      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have reason to believe that this issue is unrelated to humanoid bones, its just a red herring because that is the place most people are going to be using that kind of hierarchy. \n\nRepro without any humanoid bones:\n\n1. Anywhere on an avatar, create a new object with two children.\n\n2. Put a physbone on the the center object and ensure that Is Animated is checked and multi-child type is set to ignore.\n\n3. Give the avatar an FX animator and animate the center object moving/rotating.\n\n5. Build and test.\n\nOn beta, the object will be locked in place and not animate.\n\nOn live, the object will animate normally.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
